            "sid": "2CH 33:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "\n",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "2KI.21.1+2KI.21.2+2KI.21.3+2KI.21.4+2KI.21.5+2KI.21.6+2KI.21.7+2KI.21.8+2KI.21.9"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "2 Kings 21.1-9",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " Manasseh was twelve years old when he began to reign, and he reigned fifty-five years in Jerusalem. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 33:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He did what was evil in the sight of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", according to the abominable practices of the nations whom the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " drove out before the people of Israel. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 33:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For he rebuilt the high places which his father Hezekiah had broken down, and erected altars to the Baals, and made Asherahs, and worshiped all the host of heaven, and served them. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 33:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he built altars in the house of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", of which the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " had said, “In Jerusalem shall my name be for ever.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 33:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he built altars for all the host of heaven in the two courts of the house of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ". ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 33:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he burned his sons as an offering in the valley of the son of Hinnom, and practiced soothsaying and augury and sorcery, and dealt with mediums and with wizards. He did much evil in the sight of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", provoking him to anger. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 33:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And the image of the idol which he had made he set in the house of God, of which God said to David and to Solomon his son, “In this house, and in Jerusalem, which I have chosen out of all the tribes of Israel, I will put my name for ever; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 33:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and I will no more remove the foot of Israel from the land which I appointed for your fathers, if only they will be careful to do all that I have commanded them, all the law, the statutes, and the ordinances given through Moses.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 33:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Manasseh seduced Judah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem, so that they did more evil than the nations whom the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " destroyed before the people of Israel.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.9"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 33:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 33:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " spoke to Manasseh and to his people, but they gave no heed. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 33:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Therefore the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " brought upon them the commanders of the army of the king of Assyria, who took Manasseh with hooks and bound him with fetters of bronze and brought him to Babylon. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 33:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And when he was in distress he entreated the favor of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " his God and humbled himself greatly before the God of his fathers. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 33:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He prayed to him, and God received his entreaty and heard his supplication and brought him again to Jerusalem into his kingdom. Then Manasseh knew that the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " was God.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.13"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 33:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 33:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Afterwards he built an outer wall for the city of David west of Gihon, in the valley, and for the entrance into the Fish Gate, and carried it round Ophel, and raised it to a very great height; he also put commanders of the army in all the fortified cities in Judah. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 33:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he took away the foreign gods and the idol from the house of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", and all the altars that he had built on the mountain of the house of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " and in Jerusalem, and he threw them outside of the city. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 33:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He also restored the altar of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " and offered upon it sacrifices of peace offerings and of thanksgiving; and he commanded Judah to serve the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " the God of Israel. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 33:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Nevertheless the people still sacrificed at the high places, but only to the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " their God.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.17"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 33:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 33:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Now the rest of the acts of Manasseh, and his prayer to his God, and the words of the seers who spoke to him in the name of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " the God of Israel, behold, they are in the Chronicles of the Kings of Israel. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 33:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And his prayer, and how God received his entreaty, and all his sin and his faithlessness, and the sites on which he built high places and set up the Asherim and the images, before he humbled himself, behold, they are written in the Chronicles of the Seers.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "33.19",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "One Ms: Gk: Heb",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "of Hozai",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 33:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "2KI.21.18"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "2 Kings 21.18",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " So Manasseh slept with his fathers, and they buried him in his house; and Amon his son reigned in his stead.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.20"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 33:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 33:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "\n",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "2KI.21.19+2KI.21.20+2KI.21.21+2KI.21.22+2KI.21.23+2KI.21.24"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "2 Kings 21.19-24",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " Amon was twenty-two years old when he began to reign, and he reigned two years in Jerusalem. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 33:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He did what was evil in the sight of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", as Manasseh his father had done. Amon sacrificed to all the images that Manasseh his father had made, and served them. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 33:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he did not humble himself before the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", as Manasseh his father had humbled himself, but this Amon incurred guilt more and more. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.33.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.33.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "24",
            "style": "v",
